# No Manual pytest Invocations
RULE: NEVER run `pytest`, `python -m pytest`, or `python -m coverage` directly. ALWAYS use `bash scripts/quality-gates.sh` to run tests.
WHY: Direct pytest invocations use the active workspace venv (.venv-workspace) which may have stale installed wheels. The QG script activates the per-repo `.venv` with editable installs, matching CI exactly. Manual runs produce false results — failures that don't exist in CI, or passes that hide CI failures.
CODEX: 06-coding-standards/quality-gates.md §Two-Pass Workflow Model

DO:
  - `bash scripts/quality-gates.sh` — full quality gate (lint + tests + typecheck + codex)
  - `bash scripts/quality-gates.sh --skip-typecheck` — skip typecheck for speed
  - Per-file targeted run: `cd <repo> && .venv/bin/pytest tests/unit/test_foo.py -q` — ONLY after QG confirmed the venv is set up (i.e., `.venv/` exists). Never from workspace root.

NEVER:
  - `pytest tests/` — uses workspace venv, may resolve wrong package versions
  - `python -m pytest` — same problem
  - `python -m pytest tests/unit/ -v` from workspace shell — uses .venv-workspace
  - Interpreting results from a manual pytest run as the ground truth for CI

## Why This Matters (Root Cause)

The workspace venv (`.venv-workspace`) is for IDE IntelliSense only — NOT for running tests.
Each repo has its own `.venv/` with editable installs of all local deps.
When you run `pytest` from the workspace shell:
  - Python resolves `import unified_market_interface` from `.venv-workspace/lib/.../site-packages/`
  - That wheel may be older than the local source
  - New symbols in source code won't exist in the wheel
  - Tests that should pass appear to fail (stale wheel pattern)
  - Tests that should fail appear to pass (wheel hides missing exports)

`bash scripts/quality-gates.sh` uses `.venv/bin/python` — the repo-local venv with `uv pip install -e .` — giving CI-faithful results.

## Exception: Targeted debugging

ONLY acceptable after verifying `.venv/` exists and has the repo installed:
```bash
cd unified-market-interface
.venv/bin/pytest tests/unit/test_foo.py -xvs  # repo-local venv, not workspace
```
Never `cd unified-market-interface && pytest tests/unit/test_foo.py` (uses workspace PATH).

## Debugging with Emulators

For targeted debugging of Layer 1.5 integration tests that need emulators:

```bash
# Start emulator first (choose one):
docker compose -f unified-trading-pm/docker/docker-compose.mock.yml up pubsub-emulator
# or: docker run -d -p 8085:8085 gcr.io/google.com/cloudsdktool/google-cloud-cli gcloud beta emulators pubsub start --host-port=0.0.0.0:8085

# Then run targeted test with emulator env var:
PUBSUB_EMULATOR_HOST=localhost:8085 cd <repo> && .venv/bin/pytest tests/integration/test_pubsub_emulator.py -xvs

# Same pattern for GCS:
STORAGE_EMULATOR_HOST=http://localhost:4443 .venv/bin/pytest tests/integration/test_gcs_emulator.py -xvs
```

**Note**: Always use per-repo `.venv` (not `.venv-workspace`) for targeted debug runs. `quality-gates.sh` handles venv activation automatically for full runs.
